---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

const links = {
  docs: 'https://struphy-hub.github.io/struphy',
  github: 'https://github.com/struphy-hub/struphy',
  tutorials: 'https://github.com/struphy-hub/struphy-tutorials',
  publications: 'https://nmpp.pages.mpcdf.de/codes/struphy/',
};

const publications = [
  {
    title: 'The linearized Vlasov–Maxwell system as a Hamiltonian system',
    authors: 'Bell, Campos Pinto, Possanner, Sonnendrücker',
    venue: 'Journal of Computational Physics (2026)',
    url: 'https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jcp.2026.114765',
  },
  {
    title: 'Variational discretizations of ideal magnetohydrodynamics in smooth regime using structure-preserving finite elements',
    authors: 'Carlier, Campos-Pinto',
    venue: 'Journal of Computational Physics (2025)',
    url: 'https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jcp.2024.113647',
  },
  {
    title: 'Geometric Particle-In-Cell discretizations of a plasma hybrid model with kinetic ions and mass-less fluid electrons',
    authors: 'Li, Campos Pinto, Holderied, Possanner, Sonnendrücker',
    venue: 'arXiv (2023)',
    url: 'https://doi.org/10.48550/arxiv.2304.01891',
  },
  {
    title: 'High-Order Structure-Preserving Algorithms for Plasma Hybrid Models',
    authors: 'Possanner, Holderied, Li, Na, Bell, Hadjout, Güçlü',
    venue: 'Lecture Notes in Computer Science (2023)',
    url: 'https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-031-38299-4_28',
  },
  {
    title: 'Magneto-hydrodynamic eigenvalue solver for axisymmetric equilibria based on smooth polar splines',
    authors: 'Holderied, Possanner',
    venue: 'Journal of Computational Physics (2022)',
    url: 'https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jcp.2022.111329',
  },
  {
    title: 'MHD-kinetic hybrid code based on structure-preserving finite elements with particles-in-cell',
    authors: 'Holderied, Possanner, Wang',
    venue: 'Journal of Computational Physics (2021)',
    url: 'https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jcp.2021.110143',
  },
];
---

<Layout
  title="Struphy — Structure-preserving plasma physics in Python"
  description="Struphy is an open-source Python package for structure-preserving simulations of fluid, kinetic, and hybrid plasma models."
>
  <main>
    <section class="hero" aria-labelledby="page-title">
      <div class="hero-copy">
        <h1 id="page-title">Structure-preserving plasma physics in Python.</h1>
        <p>
          Struphy is an open-source framework for solving fluid, kinetic, and hybrid
          plasma models with geometric finite elements and Lagrangian particles.
        </p>
        <div class="actions">
          <a class="button primary" href={links.docs}>Get started</a>
          <a class="button secondary" href={links.github}>View on GitHub</a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <figure>
        <img
          src="/images/gvec-domain.webp"
          width="1800"
          height="1400"
          alt="Curved wireframe GVEC unit domain generated with Struphy"
        />
        <figcaption>GVEC unit domain generated with Struphy.</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </section>

    <section class="explainer" aria-labelledby="explainer-title">
      <h2 id="explainer-title">What "structure-preserving" means</h2>
      <p class="intro">
        Many plasma physics PDEs carry exact invariants: energy, mass, and the
        divergence-free condition on magnetic fields among them. Standard discretizations
        can violate these invariants over long simulations, letting numerical error
        accumulate. Struphy instead builds its finite-element and particle discretizations
        from a discrete de Rham complex, so these structural properties hold exactly at
        the discrete level, not only in the limit of vanishing grid size.
      </p>

      <figure class="derham">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 780 140" role="img" aria-labelledby="derham-title derham-desc">
          <title id="derham-title">The discrete de Rham complex</title>
          <desc id="derham-desc">
            Four compatible finite-element spaces are connected by the gradient, curl, and
            divergence operators: H1 maps to H(curl) via grad, H(curl) maps to H(div) via curl,
            and H(div) maps to L2 via div. Because these discrete spaces and operators commute
            exactly with their continuous counterparts, identities such as curl grad equals zero
            and div curl equals zero hold to machine precision, not just approximately.
          </desc>
          {[
            { x: 20, label: 'H¹', sub: 'scalar potentials' },
            { x: 220, label: 'H(curl)', sub: 'electric field' },
            { x: 440, label: 'H(div)', sub: 'magnetic field' },
            { x: 660, label: 'L²', sub: 'mass density' },
          ].map((node) => (
            <g transform={`translate(${node.x} 30)`}>
              <rect width="100" height="60" rx="4" class="node" />
              <text x="50" y="30" text-anchor="middle" class="node-label">{node.label}</text>
              <text x="50" y="46" text-anchor="middle" class="node-sub">{node.sub}</text>
            </g>
          ))}
          {[
            { x1: 122, x2: 218, label: 'grad' },
            { x1: 342, x2: 438, label: 'curl' },
            { x1: 562, x2: 658, label: 'div' },
          ].map((edge) => (
            <g>
              <line x1={edge.x1} y1="60" x2={edge.x2} y2="60" class="edge" marker-end="url(#arrow)" />
              <text x={(edge.x1 + edge.x2) / 2} y="50" text-anchor="middle" class="edge-label">{edge.label}</text>
            </g>
          ))}
          <defs>
            <marker id="arrow" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="6" markerHeight="6" orient="auto-start-reverse">
              <path d="M0 0L10 5L0 10z" class="arrowhead" />
            </marker>
          </defs>
        </svg>
        <figcaption>
          Discrete fields live in compatible finite-element spaces linked by exact discrete
          operators, so identities like ∇·(∇×E) = 0 hold precisely, not just approximately.
        </figcaption>
      </figure>
    </section>

    <section class="overview" aria-labelledby="models-title">
      <h2 id="models-title">Models</h2>
      <p class="intro">
        A common numerical framework supports several descriptions of plasma
        dynamics while preserving their underlying geometric structure.
      </p>
      <div class="model-list">
        <article>
          <h3>Fluid</h3>
          <p>Maxwell, MHD, and multi-fluid systems using compatible finite elements.</p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <h3>Kinetic</h3>
          <p>Vlasov and drift-kinetic models represented by Lagrangian particles.</p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <h3>Hybrid</h3>
          <p>Coupled field-particle descriptions, including MHD-kinetic models.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="quick-start" aria-labelledby="quick-start-title">
      <div>
        <h2 id="quick-start-title">Quick start</h2>
        <p>Install Struphy and compile its performance-critical kernels.</p>
        <p class="more">
          Continue with the <a href={links.docs}>installation guide</a> and
          <a href={links.tutorials}>tutorials</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="code-block">
        <button type="button" class="copy-button" data-copy-button aria-label="Copy installation commands">Copy</button>
        <pre aria-label="Struphy installation commands"><code data-copy-source><span>$</span> pip install struphy
<span>$</span> struphy compile</code></pre>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="publications" aria-labelledby="publications-title">
      <h2 id="publications-title">Publications</h2>
      <p class="intro">
        A selection of papers describing the methods and algorithms behind Struphy. See the
        <a href={links.publications}>full publication list</a> for more.
      </p>
      <ul class="publication-list">
        {publications.map((pub) => (
          <li>
            <a href={pub.url}>{pub.title}</a>
            <p class="pub-meta">{pub.authors} — {pub.venue}</p>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ul>
    </section>

    <aside class="next-page" aria-label="Domains">
      <strong>Geometry:</strong> <a href="/domains/">Explore domains</a> used by Struphy models.
    </aside>
  </main>
</Layout>

<script>
  function mountCopyButton() {
    const button = document.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-copy-button]');
    const source = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-copy-source]');
    if (!button || !source) return;

    button.onclick = async () => {
      const text = source.innerText.replace(/\$\s?/g, '').trim();
      try {
        await navigator.clipboard.writeText(text);
        button.textContent = 'Copied';
        setTimeout(() => { button.textContent = 'Copy'; }, 1800);
      } catch {
        button.textContent = 'Copy failed';
        setTimeout(() => { button.textContent = 'Copy'; }, 1800);
      }
    };
  }

  mountCopyButton();
  document.addEventListener('astro:page-load', mountCopyButton);
</script>

<style>
  .hero {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 0.92fr) minmax(380px, 1.08fr);
    gap: clamp(40px, 7vw, 88px);
    align-items: center;
    padding-block: clamp(64px, 9vw, 112px);
  }

  h1,
  h2,
  h3,
  p {
    margin-top: 0;
  }

  h1 {
    max-width: 680px;
    margin-bottom: 24px;
    font-size: clamp(2.35rem, 5vw, 4.35rem);
    line-height: 1.07;
    letter-spacing: -0.035em;
  }

  .hero-copy > p {
    max-width: 620px;
    margin-bottom: 0;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 1.1rem;
  }

  .actions {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 12px;
    margin-top: 32px;
  }

  .button {
    display: inline-block;
    padding: 10px 17px;
    border: 1px solid var(--cyan);
    color: var(--paper);
    font-weight: 650;
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .button.primary {
    background: var(--cyan);
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  .button:hover {
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 0.2em;
  }

  figure {
    margin: 0;
  }

  figure img {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
  }

  figcaption {
    margin-top: 10px;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.85rem;
  }

  .explainer,
  .overview,
  .quick-start,
  .publications {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
    padding-block: clamp(48px, 7vw, 76px);
  }

  h2 {
    margin-bottom: 12px;
    font-size: clamp(1.65rem, 3vw, 2.25rem);
    line-height: 1.2;
  }

  .intro {
    max-width: 720px;
    color: var(--muted);
  }

  .explainer .intro {
    font-size: 1.05rem;
  }

  .derham {
    margin: 32px 0 0;
    max-width: 100%;
  }

  .derham svg {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 780px;
    height: auto;
  }

  .derham .node {
    fill: var(--accent-wash);
    stroke: var(--cyan);
    stroke-width: 1.2;
  }

  .derham .node-label {
    fill: var(--paper);
    font: 700 15px var(--mono);
  }

  .derham .node-sub {
    fill: var(--muted);
    font: 10px var(--sans);
  }

  .derham .edge {
    stroke: var(--cyan);
    stroke-width: 1.4;
  }

  .derham .edge-label {
    fill: var(--muted);
    font: italic 12px var(--sans);
  }

  .derham .arrowhead {
    fill: var(--cyan);
  }

  .derham figcaption {
    margin-top: 4px;
  }

  .publication-list {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0;
    margin: 30px 0 0;
    padding: 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
    list-style: none;
  }

  .publication-list li {
    padding: 16px 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }

  .publication-list a {
    color: var(--paper);
    font-weight: 600;
    text-decoration: none;
    text-underline-offset: 0.2em;
  }

  .publication-list a:hover {
    color: var(--cyan);
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  .pub-meta {
    margin: 4px 0 0;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.85rem;
  }

  .model-list {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    gap: 0;
    margin-top: 38px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }

  .model-list article {
    padding: 28px 30px 0 0;
  }

  .model-list article + article {
    padding-left: 30px;
    border-left: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }

  h3 {
    margin-bottom: 8px;
    font-size: 1.15rem;
  }

  .model-list p,
  .quick-start p {
    color: var(--muted);
  }

  .quick-start {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: clamp(36px, 8vw, 96px);
    align-items: start;
  }

  .quick-start p {
    margin-bottom: 8px;
  }

  .more {
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  .code-block {
    position: relative;
  }

  pre {
    max-width: 100%;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 22px 24px;
    overflow-x: auto;
    border: 1px solid var(--rule);
    background: var(--code-bg);
    color: var(--paper);
    font: 0.95rem/1.9 var(--mono);
  }

  code span {
    color: var(--cyan);
  }

  .copy-button {
    position: absolute;
    top: 10px;
    right: 10px;
    padding: 5px 10px;
    border: 1px solid var(--rule);
    background: var(--ink);
    color: var(--muted);
    cursor: pointer;
    font: 600 0.75rem/1.4 var(--sans);
  }

  .copy-button:hover { color: var(--paper); border-color: var(--cyan); }

  .next-page {
    padding: 20px 0 48px;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  .next-page strong {
    color: var(--paper);
  }

  .next-page a {
    color: var(--cyan);
    text-underline-offset: 0.2em;
  }

  @media (max-width: 760px) {
    .hero {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      padding-block: 56px;
    }

    figure {
      max-width: 600px;
    }

    .model-list,
    .quick-start {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .model-list article,
    .model-list article + article {
      padding: 24px 0;
      border-left: 0;
      border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);
    }

    .quick-start {
      gap: 24px;
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 400px) {
    h1 {
      font-size: 2.15rem;
    }

    .actions {
      align-items: stretch;
      flex-direction: column;
    }

    .button {
      text-align: center;
    }

    pre {
      padding: 18px 16px;
      font-size: 0.82rem;
    }
  }
</style>
